  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Marsabit Drought Emergency Response 2017 - Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is Phase 2 of DEC and CAFOD Appeal funded Drought Emergency Response project in the Diocese of Marsabit.  In this second phase, the project targets to reach people and communities devastated by the prolonged drought in Marsabit diocese which has resulted in food insecurity and water &amp; pasture shortages.  The drought situation was declared a national disaster by the Government of Kenya in February 2017, and appealed for international support to save the lives of vulnerable people threatened by drought.  Phase 2 response strategy will involve building on DEC Phase 1.  The project will focusing on increasing access to clean and safe drinking water for water stressed remote communities, facilitating access to life saving food through cash transfer modalities, supporting secondary school children to continue attending school during the next six months through food for fees and reducing resource based conflicts  among communities in Marsabit County
Phase 2 key outcomes are:
&#x2022;	Improved access to safe and clean water to 4156 drought affected persons in Marsabit county for domestic and productive use
&#x2022;	Sustained school attendance of 100 emergency affected secondary school children in Marsabit county  
&#x2022;	Increased access to food for 3360 drought stricken persons in 6 months
&#x2022;	Decreased resource based conflict in target areas by end of 12 months
&#x2022;	Enhanced accountability to 1080 drought affected individuals through advocacy, strengthened coordination mechanism in Marsabit county in 12 months

In Phase 1 of DEC funded project, Caritas Marsabit targeted vulnerable households including 4,440 persons with emergency food distribution, 3,042 persons with Cash for work, 3,300 persons with unconditional cash transfer and 1,200 persons with water trucking. The interventions alleviated the suffering of the vulnerable persons in hard-hit villages of Diocese of Marsabit</narrative>
  </description>
